  "sourceFacts": [
    "For quiz/survey cards, compileFullShowPreviewTimeline adds question before answerCards, voting, voteLocked and results.",
    "The server maps this timeline into inventory chapters in the original order.",
    "fullShowCardNavigation takes the first chapter for each card and assigns navigation.current to that first chapter for the selected card.",
    "The Replay handler calls preview(selection(frame,navigation.current?.id),true). Consequently Replay on this question card targets :question even if the displayed phase has advanced to voting."
  ],
  "correction": "This source evidence supersedes the earlier provisional possibility that explicit Replay after a phase advance could target :voting. The earlier raw observation is preserved unchanged for provenance.",
  "conclusion": "The recorded :voting result is consistent with automatic progression and cannot be the explicit question-card Replay handler's intended response. The any-epoch wait can therefore observe a same-question automatic transition while its retained DOM remains connected.",
  "limits": [
    "Canonical failure metadata still does not prove whether the ordinary Replay click was delivered to its handler.",
    "No explicit :question Replay response is visible in the inspected candidate call window; this does not establish a pending request without an event or request record.",
    "The raw ordinal association lacks a direct request-to-result correlation. This clarification supports a source-level assertion ambiguity, not acceptance of the failed release gate."
  ]
}
